{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T00:14:49.678Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c3d835edba106c1302b3106","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.291","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-3orq"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Reconcile duplicate-event semantics between the identical-blob shortcut and the append-only history union"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"mergeTrees keeps one copy when both sides changed a history blob to the same id (git's identical-blob rule), while mergeAppendOnlyLog (since the PR #91 review fix for 4183822298) keeps one occurrence per side, so a byte-identical event appended on both sides survives twice when the sides differ elsewhere. The outcome therefore depends on unrelated edits. Byte-identical pm events (same ms timestamp, author, op, patch) on two branches realistically come from a cherry-pick or the same commit merged into both, where duplication would replay one event twice. Decide one rule (likely: dedupe byte-identical appended events) and apply it in both paths, validated against the pm CLI's own pm-history merge driver on real (hash-chain-valid) events."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["history","merge","semantics"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-07T00:14:49.678Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T00:14:49.678Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-orchestrator"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Same-input merges give the same history whether or not the two blobs are identical; the chosen rule is checked against pm's pm-history driver on real pm-written events; tests cover cherry-picked events and genuinely distinct events with equal content"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"engine/rewrite.ts","scope":"project"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"f912a9e6589145faf80213e00e03d4f847a568902c7030d8c677c79428a15318","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8bfc02ae5f0f2ad31aff47505f24521ddfbfc06767f81323291faf6020e86ae7"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T01:38:18.732Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c3d835edba106c1302b3106","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.291","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Event identity is the byte-exact JSONL line. For a shared base and two sides: (1) an event present in the base appears exactly once; (2) an event appended on only one side appears exactly once; (3) a byte-identical event appended on both sides appears exactly once (cherry-pick or the same commit merged into both), whether or not the two blobs are otherwise identical; (4) distinct appended events from both sides all appear, base kept as a strict prefix. The identical-blob shortcut and mergeAppendOnlyLog produce the same result for every case. The rule is checked against the pm CLI's pm-history merge driver on hash-chain-valid pm-written events, and tests cover cases 1-4."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T01:38:18.732Z"}],"before_hash":"f912a9e6589145faf80213e00e03d4f847a568902c7030d8c677c79428a15318","after_hash":"6efb56daa2f2e8d9af6c640df2db0cbcf4223e1f379a8d500855bc9410a104b6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a6417c8b4e32d7f93e969f6b1ee73562b446a991e64d95615306c97a72ad9a2f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T02:41:00.117Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c3d835edba106c1302b3106","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.291","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Event identity is the byte-exact JSONL line; results are a multiset union over a shared base. (1) Base occurrences are kept exactly, including repeated identical lines, and the base stays a strict prefix. (2) Lines appended on only one side keep that side's multiplicity, so two identical appends on one side stay two (as test/review-findings.test.ts expects). (3) A line appended on both sides appears max(countA, countB) times, so a cherry-picked or doubly merged event appears once, not twice, whether or not the two blobs are otherwise identical. (4) Distinct appended events from both sides all appear. The identical-blob shortcut and mergeAppendOnlyLog produce the same result in every case; the rule is checked against the pm CLI's pm-history merge driver on hash-chain-valid pm-written events, and tests cover cases 1-4 including repeated lines in the base and on one side."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T02:41:00.117Z"}],"before_hash":"6efb56daa2f2e8d9af6c640df2db0cbcf4223e1f379a8d500855bc9410a104b6","after_hash":"a63cacab1eb4dc2cf3fb0892191c73a3284aa0d3860356d606a14e86b1e92272","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"923f